or discussion, maybe bring up candidate A or D further, or reaffirm B. Also need to ensure all candidates have been covered. A was mentioned earlier by Agent 3 in round 1, but not discussed much after. D was discussed by Agent 1. C just discussed. So all four have been covered. We can now finalize recommendation. Perhaps we can argue that B remains best, but we might want to ask for clarification on any missing info? But we must not ask external info. We can just give final recommendation.\n\nWe should reference prior points: Agent 3 agreed B, noted C's strengths but concerns. Agent 1 highlighted D's strengths but concerns. We can now weigh A's profile: A can anticipate dangerous situations, see complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership qualities, but regarded as a show-off, not open to new ideas. Also A is regarded as a show-off and not open to new ideas, which are cooperation concerns. So A's leadership is offset by poor openness and show-off attitude. So B still best.\n\nThus we will state we maintain recommendation for B, summarizing why B outweighs others.\n\nProvide metadata vote Candidate B.\n\nProceed."}
